From 3b88d3be58d9e5c497e4ead394839365dd4e6345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:22:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): park cards behind one shared external blocker
 and probe it once [daveey]

Workers can tag kanban_block / kanban_continue with blocker_id when the wall is
outside their card (CI billing, an outage). While that blocker is open the
dispatcher spawns one probe card per kanban.shared_blocker_probe_seconds
(default 1800; a human unblock lets that card probe at once) and holds the rest
with respawn guard reason shared_blocker. A probe that ends without the id
clears it: held cards dispatch and blocked ones are unblocked automatically.
Probe re-assertions do not count toward the unblock-loop triage limit. Worker
context lists open blockers so later cards reuse the id.

State is derived from task_runs metadata (no schema change). Coach proposal
2026-10-19-5: 93 runs ($460) on 20 cards each rediscovering the same GitHub
Actions billing refusal.
